      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\n`compile/fullgraph/test_basic_correctness.py::test_compile_correctness[*-test_setting1]` (BAAI/bge-multilingual-gemma2) fails on XPU before running anything:\r\n\r\n```\r\nValueError: Free memory on device xpu:0 (22.18/22.71 GiB) on startup is less than desired GPU memory utilization (0.98, 22.26 GiB).\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe test passes `--gpu-memory-utilization 0.98`; an XPU device has ~0.5 GiB already reserved at startup, so the startup free-memory check rejects it. Use 0.95 on XPU only (CUDA/ROCm keep 0.98).\r\n\r\nNot a duplicate: searched open vllm-project/vllm PRs for `test_compile_correctness gpu-memory-utilization XPU`; none found.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan / Result\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nVLLM_TEST_DEVICE=xpu pytest -q \"compile/fullgraph/test_basic_correctness.py::test_compile_correctness[False-test_setting1]\"\r\nVLLM_TEST_DEVICE=xpu pytest -q \"compile/fullgraph/test_basic_correctness.py::test_compile_correctness[True-test_setting1]\"\r\n```\r\nBefore: `[False-test_setting1]` fails with the ValueError above. After: both `1 passed` (399s and 453s).\r\n\r\n## AI assistance\r\n\r\nWritten with AI assistance (GitHub Copilot CLI); I reviewed the change and ran the tests above.\r\n",
